  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115962",
      "title": "Building a Pipe That Sorts Items",
      "lectureOrder": 171,
      "videoOrder": 163,
      "sourceHash": "8e36c888b25cd43228da1292c4133dc5702287dd79462f52c6e0a40b209e1aea",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 3.3,
          "en": "So the temperature pipe is an example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.3,
          "end": 5.19,
          "en": "for a custom pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.19,
          "end": 8.28,
          "en": "I did mention before that the input value can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.28,
          "end": 9.54,
          "en": "in the end be anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.54,
          "end": 13.353,
          "en": "It can be a string, a number, but also an object or array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.22,
          "end": 18.9,
          "en": "And indeed, I now wanna build a never second pipe here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.9,
          "end": 22.26,
          "en": "which will take a more complex input value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.26,
          "end": 26.16,
          "en": "and which will also have a special behavior we haven't seen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.16,
          "end": 28.08,
          "en": "in this pipe here yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.08,
          "end": 30.66,
          "en": "And therefore here, I'll generate that pipe with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.66,
          "end": 34.68,
          "en": "of the CLI with the NGP command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.68,
          "end": 36.3,
          "en": "And I'll then name it sort",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.3,
          "end": 38.37,
          "en": "because I wanna create a pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.37,
          "end": 41.85,
          "en": "that automatically sorts an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.85,
          "end": 45.033,
          "en": "and displays the sorted array on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.05,
          "end": 48.78,
          "en": "And I'll add --skip-tests so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.78,
          "end": 50.523,
          "en": "that I don't get the testing file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.11,
          "end": 55.35,
          "en": "With that, I got this sort pipe TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.35,
          "end": 57.81,
          "en": "which gives me that class with that interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.81,
          "end": 60.393,
          "en": "and that method and that decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.58,
          "end": 66.15,
          "en": "Now here as mentioned, I want to get an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.15,
          "end": 69.93,
          "en": "and to be precise, it should be an array of strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.93,
          "end": 73.5,
          "en": "Or actually I want to accept both an array of strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.5,
          "end": 75.09,
          "en": "or an array of numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.09,
          "end": 79.203,
          "en": "So again, two possible input values of different types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.33,
          "end": 85.26,
          "en": "In addition, I also want to accept one parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.26,
          "end": 89.25,
          "en": "direction parameter, which should be either ASC",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.25,
          "end": 92.43,
          "en": "for ascending or DSC for descending.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.43,
          "end": 94.53,
          "en": "And the default value should be ascending.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.55,
          "end": 99.18,
          "en": "So that's how you can set a default value to a parameter so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.18,
          "end": 101.4,
          "en": "that the parameter becomes optional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.4,
          "end": 105.093,
          "en": "and will assume this value if it's not set by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.35,
          "end": 109.83,
          "en": "Then I'll remove this return type here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.83,
          "end": 112.08,
          "en": "That is how you could define a return type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.08,
          "end": 113.72999999999999,
          "en": "for a method in TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.72999999999999,
          "end": 114.87,
          "en": "but I'll remove it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.87,
          "end": 119.643,
          "en": "to let TypeScript infer the return type from my code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.47,
          "end": 125.814,
          "en": "Because in my code I'll now start by creating a copy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.814,
          "end": 128.403,
          "en": "of the input array here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.6,
          "end": 133.95,
          "en": "which I'll store in a constant name sorted, which I create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.95,
          "end": 136.2,
          "en": "by creating a new array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.2,
          "end": 139.71,
          "en": "And then I'll use the JavaScript spread operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.71,
          "end": 141.9,
          "en": "to copy all array elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.9,
          "end": 144.873,
          "en": "of the input array into this new array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.4,
          "end": 148.07999999999998,
          "en": "And I'm creating that copy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.07999999999998,
          "end": 151.98,
          "en": "because I want to call the sort method the built-in sort",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.98,
          "end": 155.73,
          "en": "method on that array and sort works such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.73,
          "end": 158.94299999999998,
          "en": "that it changes the array on which it's called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.78,
          "end": 162.09,
          "en": "So it does not return a new array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.09,
          "end": 165.6,
          "en": "but it changes the array on what you call it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.6,
          "end": 169.59,
          "en": "And I don't wanna change the input value array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.59,
          "end": 172.5,
          "en": "because that could mess it up in some component data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.5,
          "end": 173.79,
          "en": "And I don't wanna do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.79,
          "end": 176.613,
          "en": "I wanna create a copy, which I then change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.87,
          "end": 180,
          "en": "The build and sort method then takes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180,
          "end": 181.77,
          "en": "a function as a argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 181.77,
          "end": 184.953,
          "en": "which itself will take two parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 186.12,
          "end": 188.73,
          "en": "And there in this function, you then have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.73,
          "end": 192.87,
          "en": "to return a value greater or smaller than zero",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.87,
          "end": 195.21,
          "en": "and that will then tell JavaScript how",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.21,
          "end": 198.78300000000002,
          "en": "to order the array items and how to move them around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.1,
          "end": 203.76,
          "en": "And therefore, here, I'll check if the direction is equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.76,
          "end": 206.253,
          "en": "to ASC for ascending,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.12,
          "end": 210.06,
          "en": "in which case I'll return the result of comparing A",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.06,
          "end": 211.383,
          "en": "with B like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.25,
          "end": 215.55,
          "en": "And if A is greater than B, I'll return one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 215.55,
          "end": 217.98,
          "en": "otherwise minus one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 217.98,
          "end": 221.46,
          "en": "This will ensure that the smaller value is moved in front",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 221.46,
          "end": 222.69299999999998,
          "en": "of the bigger value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 223.56,
          "end": 226.05,
          "en": "and JavaScript will execute this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 226.05,
          "end": 228.57,
          "en": "for all value pairs of that array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.57,
          "end": 230.373,
          "en": "and move them around accordingly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 231.84,
          "end": 232.95,
          "en": "In the else case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 232.95,
          "end": 237.6,
          "en": "that the direction is descending, I'll do the opposite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 237.6,
          "end": 240.75,
          "en": "I'll return minus one if A is greater than B",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 240.75,
          "end": 242.403,
          "en": "and one otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.89,
          "end": 249.27,
          "en": "Well and then we can return this sorted array here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 249.27,
          "end": 251.13,
          "en": "So that this transfer method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.13,
          "end": 255.51,
          "en": "of this pipe returns a new sorted array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 255.51,
          "end": 259.71,
          "en": "That is now another pipe, another example for a pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 259.71,
          "end": 262.23,
          "en": "And in the end, there's nothing special about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.23,
          "end": 264.45,
          "en": "that pipe except for the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 264.45,
          "end": 267.873,
          "en": "that it takes a slightly more complex input value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 269.43,
          "end": 272.37,
          "en": "But I'll now also use it in a different place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 272.37,
          "end": 274.14,
          "en": "than I did before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 274.14,
          "end": 276.39,
          "en": "Because before I used the pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 276.39,
          "end": 281.01,
          "en": "in string interpolation to transform some value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 281.01,
          "end": 283.32,
          "en": "that's displayed on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 283.32,
          "end": 287.19,
          "en": "And now I want to use this newly added sort pipe here in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 287.19,
          "end": 290.67,
          "en": "this for loop because I wanna change this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 290.67,
          "end": 292.83,
          "en": "through which we loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 292.83,
          "end": 297.153,
          "en": "And thankfully you can use pipes there as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 298.05,
          "end": 300.75,
          "en": "You can also use them here in for loops.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 300.75,
          "end": 305.75,
          "en": "You can in general use them in your template in any place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 305.814,
          "end": 307.83,
          "en": "where you are outputting some dynamic code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 307.83,
          "end": 311.823,
          "en": "So where you are using Angular features, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 313.59,
          "end": 315.15,
          "en": "By adding this pipe symbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 315.15,
          "end": 318.453,
          "en": "and then the pipe name, sort for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 320.22,
          "end": 323.07,
          "en": "And just as before, it must be unlocked by going",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 323.07,
          "end": 325.38,
          "en": "to the imports array of the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 325.38,
          "end": 329.433,
          "en": "and by then importing the sort pipe also up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 333.12,
          "end": 334.59000000000003,
          "en": "With that, it's available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 334.59000000000003,
          "end": 337.8,
          "en": "and it will sort the items in this array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 337.8,
          "end": 340.89300000000003,
          "en": "and it's then sort at least through which we will loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 343.02,
          "end": 345.84000000000003,
          "en": "So if now save that, you can tell that this is now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 345.84000000000003,
          "end": 349.26,
          "en": "by default sorted in ascending order from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 349.26,
          "end": 351.123,
          "en": "smallest to biggest.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 352.26,
          "end": 353.64,
          "en": "And if we wanted to change this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 353.64,
          "end": 355.931,
          "en": "we could simply pass an argument to sort",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 355.931,
          "end": 359.133,
          "en": "and set this to desc for descending.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 361.02,
          "end": 364.65,
          "en": "And with that it would be sorted in the other way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 364.65,
          "end": 367.71,
          "en": "But here's something interesting now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 367.71,
          "end": 370.62,
          "en": "Do you remember that you could click these items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 370.62,
          "end": 372.66,
          "en": "to trigger on reset,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 372.66,
          "end": 377.55,
          "en": "and if you do so, that would reset the value to 18?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 377.55,
          "end": 381.75,
          "en": "Well, if you try this now, now that we're using the pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 381.75,
          "end": 385.136,
          "en": "you'll see that nothing changes as I click here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 385.136,
          "end": 387.21,
          "en": "The value is not changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 387.21,
          "end": 390.27,
          "en": "We also don't have an 18 at the bottom or a top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 390.27,
          "end": 393.78,
          "en": "Nothing changed here. I can click as often as I want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 393.78,
          "end": 398.46,
          "en": "So clearly something broke here with this new pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 398.46,
          "end": 403.14300000000003,
          "en": "and it's now time to fix it and understand why it broke.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
